# Example server-local topology overrides.
#
# Copy to "${SF_DEPLOY_ROOT}/deploy.env" (default /home/ubuntu/apps/start-first/deploy.env)
# and edit. deploy/env.sh PARSES this file as KEY=value; it is never `source`d, so
# it cannot execute code. Precedence: explicit environment > this file > defaults.
#
# It exists so that a plain `deploy/deploy.sh` re-run reproduces the intended
# bindings instead of silently reverting to loopback-only.

# --- loopback only (most restrictive; correct for a reverse-proxy/HTTPS setup) ---
# SF_BIND=127.0.0.1
# SF_PORT=8081
# SF_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081

# --- trusted LAN access over plain HTTP (current deployment) -------------------
# 0.0.0.0 covers loopback + the LAN interface + Docker bridges. Prefer this over
# pinning a single address when that address is DHCP-assigned (`ip -4 addr show`):
# a pinned address that changes makes the container fail to start with
# "cannot assign requested address" — including on loopback. See GOTCHA-020.
SF_BIND=0.0.0.0
SF_PORT=8081
SF_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081

# --- pin one address (ONLY with a static IP) ----------------------------------
# SF_BIND=127.0.0.1 192.168.169.223
# SF_PORT=8081
# SF_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081
